From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:38:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ether: volume panel by the keys, and finish the CNE property
 access

Three things, all small.

sepolicy: CNEService reads the same properties cnd does, and giving persist.cne.* and
persist.vendor.cnd.* their own type in 0031 moved them out of its reach as well --

    avc: denied { read } comm=".dataservices" scontext=u:r:dataservice_app:s0
                         tcontext=u:object_r:vendor_cne_prop:s0

so the framework half of CNE lost access that relabelling was never meant to take. Same rule, same
type. The app is hosted in the .dataservices process, which is why it does not show up as "cne" in
ps and is easy to believe dead.

persist.vendor.cnd.iwlan: CNE's own IWLAN switch, read by libcne, unset by this port and by stock.
Worth setting only now that 0031 lets CNE read that property space -- the measured effect of 0031
was "pref data tech UNKNOWN" becoming "pref data tech LTE", so CNE is answering; IWLAN is still not
among the candidates it prepares, and this is the switch named for it. persist.vendor.cnd.wqe is
the other one libcne reads and is deliberately left alone, so a change in the candidate list has a
single cause.

Volume panel: put it on the left, where this device's volume keys are, and raise it to meet them.
The rocker sits at about 31% of screen height, not the middle -- fitting a homography from a photo
to screen coordinates puts the two keys at y 505 and y 694 of 1920, midpoint 600, against the
panel's own centre of 961. Hence -180dp. def_volume_panel_on_left is a first-boot default only;
Settings > System > Buttons > "Show panel on left" still wins for anyone who changes it.
---
 device.mk                                             | 11 +++++++++++
 .../base/packages/SystemUI/res/values/dimens.xml      | 11 +++++++++++
 .../LineageSettingsProvider/res/values/defaults.xml   |  7 +++++++
 sepolicy/cnd.te                                       |  9 +++++++++
 4 files changed, 38 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 overlay/frameworks/base/packages/SystemUI/res/values/dimens.xml
 create mode 100644 overlay/lineage-sdk/packages/LineageSettingsProvider/res/values/defaults.xml

diff --git a/device.mk b/device.mk
index b38fb03..617af76 100644
--- a/device.mk
+++ b/device.mk
@@ -403,6 +403,17 @@ PRODUCT_PROPERTY_OVERRIDES += ro.telephony.block_binder_thread_on_incoming_calls
 #   persist.radio.VT_CAM_INTERFACE -- video telephony is deliberately off (config_device_vt_available).
 PRODUCT_PROPERTY_OVERRIDES += persist.data.iwlan.enable=true
 
+# CNE's own IWLAN switch, read by libcne alongside persist.cne.feature. Left unset by this port and
+# by stock. It is only worth setting now that sepolicy lets CNE read that property space at all --
+# before device 0031 the daemon could not see any persist.cne.*/persist.vendor.cnd.* name, so this
+# would have been another property set and never read.
+#
+# The measured effect of 0031 was CNE going from "pref data tech UNKNOWN" to "pref data tech LTE".
+# IWLAN still does not appear among the candidates it prepares, and this is the switch named for it.
+# persist.vendor.cnd.wqe is the other one libcne reads and is deliberately not set yet: one at a
+# time, so a change in the candidate list has a single cause.
+PRODUCT_PROPERTY_OVERRIDES += persist.vendor.cnd.iwlan=true
+
 # nanopb 0.2.8, for libril-qc-qmi-1.so alone. See nanopb-0.2.8/Android.bp for why a second copy of
 # nanopb has to exist at all.
 PRODUCT_PACKAGES += libnanopb_legacy
diff --git a/overlay/frameworks/base/packages/SystemUI/res/values/dimens.xml b/overlay/frameworks/base/packages/SystemUI/res/values/dimens.xml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..01e386d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/overlay/frameworks/base/packages/SystemUI/res/values/dimens.xml
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
+<resources>
+    <!-- The Robin's volume rocker is at roughly 31% of the screen's height, not the middle, so the
+         stock centred panel sits well below the keys being pressed. Measured by fitting a
+         homography from a photo of the device to screen coordinates using four on-screen landmarks:
+         the two buttons come out at y 505 and y 694 of 1920, midpoint 600. The panel's own centre
+         is 961 (it spans 607..1315), so it wants to come up 361px, which is 180dp at this density.
+         An independent check point held back from the fit landed 2.4% of screen height out, which
+         is the accuracy to expect here. -->
+    <dimen name="volume_dialog_offset_y">-180dp</dimen>
+</resources>
diff --git a/overlay/lineage-sdk/packages/LineageSettingsProvider/res/values/defaults.xml b/overlay/lineage-sdk/packages/LineageSettingsProvider/res/values/defaults.xml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..65e87f3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/overlay/lineage-sdk/packages/LineageSettingsProvider/res/values/defaults.xml
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
+<resources>
+    <!-- The volume keys are on the Robin's left edge, so put the panel on the same side. This is a
+         first-boot default only: it seeds the settings database when it is created, and anyone who
+         changes it under Settings > System > Buttons > "Show panel on left" keeps their choice. -->
+    <bool name="def_volume_panel_on_left">true</bool>
+</resources>
diff --git a/sepolicy/cnd.te b/sepolicy/cnd.te
index 29bd066..2964d4b 100644
--- a/sepolicy/cnd.te
+++ b/sepolicy/cnd.te
@@ -10,3 +10,12 @@
 # libcne reads to find the WLAN interface it is supposed to be evaluating.
 get_prop(cnd, vendor_cne_prop)
 get_prop(cnd, wifi_hal_prop)
+
+# CNEService, the framework half of the Connectivity Engine, reads the same properties. It is not a
+# separate concern from the rule above: giving persist.cne.* and persist.vendor.cnd.* their own type
+# moved them out of default_prop, which this domain could read, so relabelling alone takes the
+# access away from it:
+#   avc: denied { read } comm=".dataservices" scontext=u:r:dataservice_app:s0
+#                        tcontext=u:object_r:vendor_cne_prop:s0
+# The app is hosted in the .dataservices process, which is why `ps | grep cne` does not find it.
+get_prop(dataservice_app, vendor_cne_prop)
